{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Predictive Feature Relevance.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Predictive Feature Relevance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"predictive feature relevance predictive feature relevance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Predictive Feature Relevance.md","fileName":"Predictive Feature Relevance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Predictive Feature Relevance","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 21:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Classification Feature Selection]] · [[Feature Engineering and Metadata]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Classification Feature Selection","Feature Engineering and Metadata","dataclassification.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Predictive Feature Relevance.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Predictive Feature Relevance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"predictive feature relevance predictive feature relevance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Predictive Feature Relevance.md","fileName":"Predictive Feature Relevance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Predictive Feature Relevance","heading":"Predictive Feature Relevance","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Predictive feature relevance is the degree to which a variable helps distinguish observations belonging to different classes. With labels available, relevance can be estimated through association, dependence, distance, or class-separation criteria.\n\nA relevant feature contributes information about the target rather than merely varying across cases. The source emphasizes that selecting discriminative features can improve generalization, reduce computation and storage, and leave the original variables interpretable.\n\nIn the book's workflow, relevance is examined alongside redundancy and operational availability. A highly ranked field can still be unsuitable if it is an identifier, leaks the target, is mostly missing, or cannot be obtained when predictions are made.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Classification Feature Selection","Feature Engineering and Metadata","dataclassification.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Predictive Feature Relevance.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Predictive Feature Relevance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"predictive feature relevance predictive feature relevance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Predictive Feature Relevance.md","fileName":"Predictive Feature Relevance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Predictive Feature Relevance","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[dataclassification.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofdatascience.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Classification Feature Selection","Feature Engineering and Metadata","dataclassification.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}